{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live","id":1468323,"title":"Trinity Continuum: Anima is live!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Anima"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-18T19:43:34-08:00","id":1468323,"title":"Trinity Continuum: Anima is live!","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/trinity-continuum-anima-tabletop-roleplaying-game\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...leplaying-game</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T20:02:43-08:00","id":1468326,"title":"","content":"Congrats on meeting the funding goal so early. You should be able to get much more before the end of the funding period if enthusiasm is this high. Very promising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T07:45:58-08:00","id":1468838,"title":"","content":"Ooof, the shipping charge to Canada is insane. A few Canadian retailers sometimes get Onyx Path products when they are released, so I'll keep an eye out as the concept of this one seems interesting. I don't mind the concept of print on demand that OP embraces, but I really wish they'd have better support and pricing for non-Americans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T08:34:03-08:00","id":1468839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1468838#post1468838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooof, the shipping charge to Canada is insane. A few Canadian retailers sometimes get Onyx Path products when they are released, so I'll keep an eye out as the concept of this one seems interesting. I don't mind the concept of print on demand that OP embraces, but I really wish they'd have better support and pricing for non-Americans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shipping costs went up considerably during COVID, and there's not a whole lot we can do about it, sorry. I'm Canadian too.<br /> <br /> Kickstarted books aren't print-on-demand, btw. They're traditionally-printed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T09:36:06-08:00","id":1468843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1468838#post1468838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooof, the shipping charge to Canada is insane. A few Canadian retailers sometimes get Onyx Path products when they are released, so I'll keep an eye out as the concept of this one seems interesting. I don't mind the concept of print on demand that OP embraces, but I really wish they'd have better support and pricing for non-Americans.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you see the shipping to Brazil, surely you will cry for me.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T04:54:18-08:00","id":1468914,"title":"","content":"For Europe it's also very high.<br /> <br /> I understand that the initial traditional print must be done in a single batch.<br /> But, the POD books could be printed closer to the destination?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> I have cheked it and is 40$ shipment everywhere.<br /> That is painful for a 55$ book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25829,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","user":"Vjornin","date":".  Checked prices 11-26-2021, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T19:36:47-08:00","id":1468939,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was looking at Anima for cyberpunk &amp; fantasy rules I could apply to Trinity's version of Storypath... but it's hard to justify a paying almost as much in shipping as the book itself. Sort of used to it being in Australia... but it does make it hard to justify at this time of year (when I have xmas to deal with too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T20:50:13-08:00","id":1468940,"title":"","content":"So get the PDF for now and then save to get the POD version","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T15:42:24-08:00","id":1469962,"title":"","content":"I'm always saddened by how little Onyx Path supports their games. Whether it be print distribution, virtual tabletop support, or really anything beyond just writing and creating PDFs. It means that for anyone outside the U.S, their games remain ultra niche and unknown. Which is a shame as their Storypath system is solid, and I've loved the Trinity universe ever since the 90s. But I know if I ask friends if they want to play, they'll ask me where to get the books. Or if there are official Roll20 modules. Or anything else other than just PDFs.<br /> <br /> I genuinely wonder if Onyx Path cares about getting their games out there, or if they just enjoy writing these for the sake of writing. But whatever. All I can do is keep hammering Google with Trinity Continuum &lt;anything&gt; Canada until something clicks. Was lucky to get Aeon and Core quick, but it took me a solid five or six months before Aberrant showed up on the radar at a nice steep price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T15:48:52-08:00","id":1469965,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#800000\">Karl, insinuating that Onyx Path doesn't care about our games, or that we don't know how to do our jobs, because you don't understand the details of how publishing works is skirting <i>very</i> close to a rule violation, I would recommend you dial it back and consider your words more carefully in the future.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T15:56:10-08:00","id":1469969,"title":"","content":"You're right. I vented. I don't think any of my points are wrong, but I do agree that I could have phrased it more diplomatically. Apologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T16:21:44-08:00","id":1469970,"title":"","content":"That said, <i>I live in Canada</i>. Ordering in Canada works about the same way it does in the US. I have never had difficulty getting any of the books I work on.<ul><li>If you get in early enough, you can pledge on Kickstarter. Shipping's a bear, but you're guaranteed your book, and you often get a lot of supplementary PDF material &quot;free&quot; which balances it out.</li> <li>If you miss the Kickstarter, you can preorder on BackerKit. Same deal but without the freebies.</li> <li>Post-campaign, the Kickstarted books can be ordered from Studio2 or Indie Press Revolution, either by you or by your local game store. IIRC Studio 2 ships through Alliance, so for most stores it can be made part of their standard order without much additional shipping cost.</li> <li>You can get PDF or print-on-demand from DriveThruRPG. DTRPG's got a printer in Markham or thereabouts, so it's domestic shipping.</li> </ul>It's the same sources that Americans have access to, except the shipping's higher on the traditionally-printed books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 12-08-2021, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T11:48:50-08:00","id":1470059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1469970#post1469970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Post-campaign, the Kickstarted books can be ordered from Studio2 or Indie Press Revolution, either by you or by your local game store. IIRC Studio 2 ships through Alliance, so for most stores it can be made part of their standard order without much additional shipping cost.</li> <li>You can get PDF or print-on-demand from DriveThruRPG. DTRPG's got a printer in Markham or thereabouts, so it's domestic shipping.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Can we get the POD books from an European printer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T11:54:36-08:00","id":1470061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vjornin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1470059#post1470059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can we get the POD books from an European printer?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, there's a PoD printer in Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T12:04:05-08:00","id":1470064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1470061#post1470061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, there's a PoD printer in Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, then I will get them when available.<br /> At the moment I have pledged for Adventure! and Anima only in pdf version because of shipping costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T01:37:54-08:00","id":1470197,"title":"","content":"How good is Anima at the moment for those of you who have been able to read the preview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T04:04:11-08:00","id":1470210,"title":"","content":"Loving it so far. The game itself has some spikes in it that makes you go &quot;Excuse me, what?&quot; and I even got a bit of existential horror at one point. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T14:31:03-08:00","id":1470242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1470197#post1470197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How good is Anima at the moment for those of you who have been able to read the preview?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reasonably good, although I do find it odd that, even though PCs are assumed to be Talents, it is literally impossible to use any of their Talent powers unless they buy the <i>In the Zone</i> Gift, which allows them to use Dramatic Editing inside the game. Similarly, psiads and novas are also incapable of using their respective powers to affect the game. While this was likely implemented to prevent players from using their special powers to ROFLSTOMP their way through Terra Surge, it comes across as heavy handed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T14:59:14-08:00","id":1470243,"title":"","content":"Not even the technology manipulating powers that Novas and Psiads have access to can do anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T17:12:36-08:00","id":1470249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1470243#post1470243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even the technology manipulating powers that Novas and Psiads have access to can do anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not from inside the game, as written, at least.<br /> I doubt Glass plays nice with either Quantum or Psi based interfaces. They weren't designed for it and the nature of the brain/Glass interface would complicate it. It is a kind of hard tech designed by a Nova that doesn't want other Aberrants to mess with it.<br /> Add that to the neural interface coding of what we could call a &quot;full dive virtual reality&quot; on what is probably hardened military grade servers...it is not easy. Heck there is a whole section on how Novas tried and failed to do what Glass does.<br /> All of that fails to take into account the real time monitoring from the AIs to boot.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it is a judgment call from the Storyteller, but the game doesn't want you to try or think it is possible<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T22:27:18-08:00","id":1470258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1470243#post1470243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even the technology manipulating powers that Novas and Psiads have access to can do anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>you (the Nova or Psiad) might be able to use such powers on the program of the game, but that wouldn\u2019t translate into your anima wielding them in the in-universe fiction of the game, which is more the issue here.<br /> <br /> That said, I\u2019ll note some things in errata I think would be appropriate allowances (for example, you shouldn\u2019t be able to use Social Gifts on TerraSurge npcs, because they\u2019re just interacting with your anima\u2019s stats, but since you use your actual social attributes and abilities to interact with other TerraSurge players, social Gifts should be as workable as with any other form of remote communication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-12-2021, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T08:38:57-08:00","id":1470280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1470258#post1470258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> you (the Nova or Psiad) might be able to use such powers on the program of the game, but that wouldn\u2019t translate into your anima wielding them in the in-universe fiction of the game, which is more the issue here.<br /> <br /> That said, I\u2019ll note some things in errata I think would be appropriate allowances (for example, you shouldn\u2019t be able to use Social Gifts on TerraSurge npcs, because they\u2019re just interacting with your anima\u2019s stats, but you since you use your actual social attributes and abilities to interact with other TerraSurge players, social Gifts should be as workable as with any other form of remote communication.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T09:44:39-08:00","id":1470282,"title":"","content":"A Nova or Psiad using technology powers over Terra Surge wold work as a GM, can move things around, give and take equipment, kill and unkill and give themselves (and others) powers beyond regular anima powers.<br /> <br /> It would be a great sourcebook one with the effects the dots in technokinesis and nova cyberkinesis powers can do inside TerraSurge.<br /> <br /> Things like being able to control NPCs, teleportation, becoming invulnerable, instant kill, hacking chats, changing your anima traits and equipment at will, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 12-12-2021, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T12:25:08-08:00","id":1470289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1470282#post1470282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Nova or Psiad using technology powers over Terra Surge wold work as a GM, can move things around, give and take equipment, kill and unkill and give themselves (and others) powers beyond regular anima powers.<br /> <br /> It would be a great sourcebook one with the effects the dots in technokinesis and nova cyberkinesis powers can do inside TerraSurge.<br /> <br /> Things like being able to control NPCs, teleportation, becoming invulnerable, instant kill, hacking chats, changing your anima traits and equipment at will, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use your powers to hack the game itself, yes - but there are 4 hyper-intelligent AIs that will immediately aggressively respond to that (remember true AIs are Nova invented tech, so they\u2019re not going to get steamrollered here).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T15:10:47-08:00","id":1470302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1470289#post1470289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could use your powers to hack the game itself, yes - but there are 4 hyper-intelligent AIs that will immediately aggressively respond to that (remember true AIs are Nova invented tech, so they\u2019re not going to get steamrollered here).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Narrators are not Nova invented, only Glass is (as far as we know). TerraSurge is not designed for Glass, it can be used and it explore the full potency of the engine, but it was created before, in another country (England if I am not wrong) by another company.<br /> <br /> I would say it was invented by Talents, so it\u2019s not going to be a easy job to hack it, but a Mega Intelligent Nova will have scale over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T15:29:32-08:00","id":1470303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1470302#post1470302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Narrators are not Nova invented, only Glass is (as far as we know). TerraSurge is not designed for Glass, it can be used and it explore the full potency of the engine, but it was created before, in another country (England if I am not wrong) by another company.<br /> <br /> I would say it was invented by Talents, so it\u2019s not going to be a easy job to hack it, but a Mega Intelligent Nova will have scale over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>True AIs as a technology were Nova invented during the Nova age, just like hyperfusion and grav crystals were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-12-2021, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T15:41:49-08:00","id":1470304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1470303#post1470303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True AIs as a technology were Nova invented during the Nova age, just like hyperfusion and grab crystals were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the Narrators themselves were not created by Novas, they were build based on a \u201csafe\u201d and \u201cwell established\u201d AI.<br /> <br /> They are not black boxes that were pointed to the right direction, the project was created by a nova, simplified into a Coretech that could be copied and modified by baselines.<br /> <br /> Knowing programmers, there must be a stack overflow about building AIs with a lot of bug fixes and simplified codes to make them lighter and running on any OS\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T17:13:47-08:00","id":1470312,"title":"","content":"This is a great discussion. Really enlightening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T19:34:52-08:00","id":1470324,"title":"","content":"I believe there was a bit in the Anima manuscript about how nova built AI are more complex than the AI that have been built since the Aberrant War.<br /> <br /> Talking about the Narrators, given that the programmers have apparently defaulted to just dumping info into them, I wonder if the mysterious Cascadia Earthquake is linked to the backstory of the Quell, who entered the game &quot;in an attempt to flee a subterranean enemy,&quot; and whether this means the AI have accidentally picked up on a slumbering Aberrant beneath the city and have just turned the knowledge into a story hook, because that is what they're programmed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T06:27:47-08:00","id":1470341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1470324#post1470324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">backstory of the Quell</div> </div> </div> </div>What is this <i><b>'Quell' </b></i>I read from time to time in manuscript parts I read? I cannot find direct definition what it should be - is it in real world, in Terra Surge? What it is? \ud83e\udd28","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T07:27:50-08:00","id":1470343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1468323-trinity-continuum-anima-is-live?p=1470341#post1470341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is this <i><b>'Quell' </b></i>I read from time to time in manuscript parts I read? I cannot find direct definition what it should be - is it in real world, in Terra Surge? What it is? \ud83e\udd28</div> </div> </div> </div>They're a Terra Surge PC race of bug-people that weren't originally supposed to be a PC race.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">They were intended to be an</span> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">antagonist NPC </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">group into</span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> which players would sometimes incarnate as a form </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">of \u201cpunishment\u201d</span> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">to mitigate the negative impact of</span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> player killer</span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">s on the overall</span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> game</span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> climate. Based on their lore,</span> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">they were meant to turn into unlikely allies against a common foe at some point down the line,</span> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">but when the developers caved in to player d</span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">emand and made them playable full time, they also</span> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">gave players the keys to this transition and how it would eventually play out.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Basically, if your player went around killing too many other players, you'd be turned into a Quell for awhile. Some players liked this, so went on killing sprees to purposefully get turned into a Quell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T13:35:55-08:00","id":1470366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https:/